# =============================================================================
# Mosquitto password file.
#
# DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE BY HAND — Mosquitto's internal hashing format is not
# stable across versions and hand-written PBKDF2 entries are almost always
# wrong.
#
# Correct workflow (inside a Mosquitto container so you get a compatible
# version of mosquitto_passwd):
#
#   docker compose run --rm broker \
#       mosquitto_passwd -c -b /mosquitto/config/passwd sim_user    sim_pass
#   docker compose run --rm broker \
#       mosquitto_passwd -b    /mosquitto/config/passwd ingest_user ingest_pass
#
# The "-c" flag CREATEs the file (drop-in first user only). Subsequent
# additions omit "-c" so existing entries are appended.
#
# For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT / DEMO ONLY the Dockerfile runs these commands
# automatically at build time using build args so `docker compose up --build`
# yields a working broker out of the box. For a production deployment
# regenerate with a strong password and never commit the hashed passwd file.
#
# Lines below are commented-out illustrative placeholders that Mosquitto
# will ignore because they start with '#'.
# =============================================================================
# sim_user:$7$101$...PBKDF2-SHA512 hash of "sim_pass"...
# ingest_user:$7$101$...PBKDF2-SHA512 hash of "ingest_pass"...
